      "message": "fix(waterjet): lay straight leads beside tabs and refuse a cut bridge\n\nThe review of PR #3058 found that arc leads beside a tab cut the tab\nfree of the sheet. An arc lead-in comes from behind its stretch start\nand an arc lead-out runs on past its stretch end - both into the tab\ngap - and their kerfs met under the tab.\n\n- plan::tabbed now leads every stretch in and out straight along the\n  waste normal (a note says so when arc leads were asked). Straight\n  leads leave the full tab width between the two lead kerfs.\n- New bridge law (tabs::bridge_law, run in emit::cut): from the part\n  edge under each gap middle, a line out along the waste normal past\n  the longest lead must stay more than the kerf radius from every lit\n  chord. Else the cut is refused by name (\"tab N holds nothing\").\n- Pins: arc_leads_beside_a_tab_leave_the_tab_joined_to_the_sheet\n  (rasters the kerf and flood-fills from the part to the sheet) and\n  the_bridge_law_refuses_a_kerf_across_a_tab.\n- The golden waterjet_tabbed_plate_with_holes.cl is pinned again: the\n  outline stretches now have straight leads at X58.6 and X61.4.\n\nRefs #1883\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
